WHY THIS CODE IS PUBLIC

Flyten is published so that it can be read. The point of putting it here is
that someone can open any file and see how the thing was actually built: the
reasoning in the comments, the decisions that were reversed, and the parts
that were measured before they were kept. Prospective employers, collaborators
and anyone curious are welcome to read all of it.

Public is not the same as free to take. The terms below say where that line
sits.


YOU MAY

  - Read, study and reference any part of this repository.
  - Clone it and run it locally to evaluate it.
  - Quote short excerpts with attribution, for example in a review, article,
    or discussion of the work.


YOU MAY NOT, WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION

  - Copy, republish or redistribute this code or substantial parts of it.
  - Use it, in whole or in part, in any product or service, commercial or
    otherwise.
  - Distribute derivative works based on it.
  - Present it, or work derived from it, as your own.

All rights not expressly granted above are reserved. Permission is reachable:
open an issue and ask.


