NOT MEDICAL ADVICE

Flyten estimates calorie and macronutrient targets from population-level
equations, principally Mifflin-St Jeor. Those equations describe an average,
and an individual's real energy expenditure can sit ten to fifteen percent
either side of the number this software returns. The training plans are
templates matched to a goal, not individual programming.

Nothing this software produces is medical or dietary advice, and nothing in it
is a substitute for a consultation. Anyone making a significant change to how
they eat or train should talk to a doctor or a registered dietitian first,
and especially so if they are managing a health condition, recovering from an
injury, pregnant, or under eighteen.
